# Components

This page is the template-layer guide for `@component`. Canonical complete
source is [Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/). Do not
copy the file into `docs/`. Forms and errors live in
[Components](/docs/reference/language/components/).

**Starting files:** `examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci`

A `@component` signature matches ordinary Roc function syntax, with a
`@component` prefix: `| { props } |` or `| { props }, content |`. Lowering
emits a function that returns `Html`. Given the same props and body, it
produces the same markup. Effects belong in `@init` and handlers. There is no
runtime component registry and no implicit instance state.

`@fixture` bindings are **experimental** syntax used to preview components
(`rocci view` / `rocci browse`) and to supply test data. They do not change
the generated component function.

## Declare and call

Names are PascalCase. Consecutive leading capitals (`HTMLShell`) are rejected;
write `HtmlShell`. The first parameter is a props record. Nested markup is a
second `Html` argument, not a `children` field. Putting `Html` in the record
wraps it in `Html.text` and escapes it.

```rocci
@component Card = |{ title }, content|
    <section>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        {content}
    </section>

@component Page = |_|
    <Card title="Hello">
        <p>Body is Html, not a string.</p>
    </Card>
```

A self-closing tag is a one-argument call. Qualified calls use the imported
module: `<Design.Button />` → `Design.button`. Missing PascalCase names fail
in Roc, not in a client-side registry.

`??` field defaults are **experimental**. Omit the field at the call site;
lowering fills it.

In the styling example, `Hello` takes `{ name ?? "Roc" }`. A self-closing
`<Hello />` uses the default. The component is **pure**: it cannot log, open
SQLite, or read the request.

## Preview with fixtures

```rocci
@fixture{target: Hello}
helloTest = { name: "Ada" }
```

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello
```

The preview shows **Hello, Ada** from `helloTest`. Pass `--arg name=Roc` to
override. HTTP declarations are ignored in `view`.

## Inspect lowering

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

The output names `Hello`, `FeatureCard`, and `StylePage`, lists the fixtures,
and prints source-map segments.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

Generated Roc contains `hello`, `featureCard`, and `stylePage`.

`rocci run` on the same file serves the full page (`@get:view("/")`). File-level
`@css` styles `body`, not `html`.

## Library layout

Put reusable widgets in `components/`. Keep page-private helpers in the same
`.rocci` module. `rocci browse components/` lists fixtures across a directory.

**Related:** [Markup](/docs/templates/markup/),
[Fixtures](/docs/reference/language/fixtures/),
[Roc](/docs/appendix/roc-for-rocci/).
